            <title>[LU-21299] recovery-small test_116: OST restart returns already mounted</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21299</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2ab7ac8a-c297-46b9-85a6-d6abe1ed9ba9" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2ab7ac8a-c297-46b9-85a6-d6abe1ed9ba9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_116 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;test_116 returned 17
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.119&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4772" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4772&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.119&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4772" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4772&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Filed by Patch Watcher's weekly branch filer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;recovery-small test_116 returns 17 in failover runs. Two independent logs, one ldiskfs and one ZFS, show the same sequence: ost1 is stopped, the no-delay statfs checks run, ost1 is mounted successfully, then lctl dl on another node reports "Writer error: failed to resolve Netlink family id". Cleanup attempts to start ost1 again and mount.lustre_tgt returns 17 because it is already mounted. This is a test restoration/facet-state symptom; the underlying cause is not established.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow window 2026-10-25 through 2026-11-23: 36 failed branch sessions. lustre-master: 24/582 suite runs (4.12%), first November 1, latest November 16. lustre-master-next: 12/679 (1.77%), November 7 through November 9. Failing groups are failover-part-1 and failover-zfs-part-1. Config rates on master are 12/15 and 12/14; on master-next, 6/15 in each group. Full-part-1 and the displayed review groups pass, so aggregate suite rates understate the failover impact.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2ab7ac8a-c297-46b9-85a6-d6abe1ed9ba9" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2ab7ac8a-c297-46b9-85a6-d6abe1ed9ba9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/026f9599-a6f2-4e09-9929-c8cc097d6eae" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/026f9599-a6f2-4e09-9929-c8cc097d6eae&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Logs:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/25d1a66a-efb3-4262-8cc1-c34051e6ac4d/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/25d1a66a-efb3-4262-8cc1-c34051e6ac4d/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/fd59df85-1ccf-454b-a2ba-b7ed5d73bd1c/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/fd59df85-1ccf-454b-a2ba-b7ed5d73bd1c/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LU searches for the test name, returned 17 and the Netlink error found no matching ticket. An open Gerrit search for test_116/Netlink touching recovery-small.sh returned no changes. EX cannot be searched with this account. No local reproduction or code change was attempted.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
